 "review": {"identity": "swe2-max-1 (Devin/SWE-2 Max)", "method": "Acceptance suite run locally with `retail,gpu,audio` (CS_GAME_DIR, CS_ENGINE_IMAGE): the `accept_flak_c_` selection's ignored windowed test drove the owner's own command `cs --cs-path $CS_GAME_DIR --mission M01 --smoke-seconds 45 --capture-dir private/evidence/FLAK-C-FLAK-ROUND-AND-EFFECT` on this machine's GPU, and the ignored headless test drove the same production chain — test wake of `aagun99` (a sleeping `wep_27` world turret no M01 program wakes; wake and placement labelled test ones in report.json), the turret runtime's retail flak rocket, the round's proximity burst, the `flak_effect` presentation (flash light, smoke ball, close-range framebuffer flicker) and the `snd_enemyflak` / `snd_missile_flak` cues — without a window. The windowed run wrote the `flak_burst` and `flak_burst_tail` framebuffer PNGs and report.json, which this report hashes as artifacts. The run is automated, never `human_play`, and no original executable ran; the wake, the placement and the presentation gating are designed, not verified_original — the trails stay undrawn because the `call_flak_trails` OBJECT_MOTION units and frame are unmeasured (FLAK-C1/C3 findings; report.json counts every such burst under `trails_undrawn`), and the burst's splash applies no damage because its falloff and the entity+0x678 factor are unmeasured (FLAK-C2). This harness derives every field from the recorded log, production discovery of $CS_GAME_DIR, the smoke's report and the hashes of those artifacts. Validated with tools/validate_evidence.py --require-pass."},
